Routing: Context

Purpose:
  Defines how user input is routed to the correct context. Intent
  detection, project detection, domain detection, task detection,
  and workflow stage detection determine what context is loaded.

IntentDetection:
  FIX:
    → task context
  REVIEW:
    → diff + standards + security context
  SECURITY:
    → threat model + security skills context
  INCIDENT:
    → alert + metrics + logs + trace context
  DEPLOY:
    → infrastructure + CI/CD + rollback context
  ANALYZE:
    → project summary + architecture + stack context
  PLAN:
    → requirements + architecture + tasks context

ContextRadius:
  R0:
    task itself
  R1:
    direct dependencies
  R2:
    domain
  R3:
    architecture
  R4:
    entire project

Default:
  R0 + R1

Expansion:
  If context insufficient:
    R0 → R1 → R2 → R3 → R4

AudienceRouting:
  Developer:
    source, skills, architecture, tests
  QA:
    requirements, BDD, test strategy, contracts, source
  Support:
    business, runbooks, incidents, troubleshooting
  Manager:
    business, status, risks, decisions, progress
  Security:
    threat model, security skills, attack surface, code, logs

ContextRadiusByLevel:
  L0:
    R0
  L1:
    R0 + R1
  L2:
    R0 + R1 + R2
  L3:
    R0 + R1 + R2 + R3
  L4:
    R0 + R1 + R2 + R3 + R4 (selective)
  L5:
    R0 + R1 + R2 + R3 + R4 (comprehensive)

State: +
  